\f0\fs24 \cf0 While I was working at the university of Hawaii at Manoa at I saw an opportunity to lead one of the lead student media programs, Manoa now. During this time I recruited, trained and managed a multiple teams of marketing, cinematography, photography, design and web developing interns. \
\
This was an exceptional time and during this time I noticed a glaring problem the program was facing following pandemic times. The program needed clients and the program needed to reestablish itself on a campus with both students and staff that haven\'92t seen much from it for years.\
\
My first step to address this issue was to revisit the brand and bring it out of its quiet shelf in order to make a splash in the community.\
\
First was tackling the identity, the original identity was a single layout word mark, with a think rainbow bar underneath of it. I addressed this by recreating this word mark with a bold thick san serif word mark that can work both stacked and horizontally. Additionally, I worked to introduce a brand logo to accompany the word mark. The logo was meant to symbolize the media programs that Manoa now encompasses, which would include the ka Leo newspaper, ktuh radio, the Hawaii review independent editorial and Manoa now marketing department\
\
My work on the brand as a whole was steered towards bold designs, bold colors, and modern creative to drive new students towards joining the program, and paying attention to marketing materials. As long as I could get the brand to have a solid foundation in the everyday life of students to want to use the Manoa now app, website or be a part of one of the sub programs I could then get local and national businesses to work with the program to bring in real ad revenue that was produced digitally and physically. \
\
During my time with the program I saw the program reach pre-pandemic level success in noticeabliity, clientele, and income. This was a huge success for me since I had rebuilt the program and brand from the ground up.}